  "comments": "Starting in the late 1990s, large quantities of manipulated Korean 500 won coins were brought into Japan. These were made of the same material, had the same diameter and now also the same weight as the 500 yen coins. They were used at vending machines to obtain genuine 500 yen coins through the refund mechanism (the won coins had only 1/10 their value).<br />\r\nThis led to the discontinuation of the production of 500 yen coins and a new version with modified alloy and anti-counterfeit designs in 2000.<br />\r\nHowever, it took a few more years before only the new coins were accepted by all vending machines.",
